A||||2||Black88GT||VERY cool fiero experience.....||||14||
Z||000000||Black88GT||10-15-2000||09:33 PM||||I love when things like this happen in my fiero. <P>I work in an "upperclass" neighborhood.  There is a local sub shop/deli that I go to for lunch everytime I work there (weekends).  Most people there thumb their noses at me since I am usually dirty and smelly (work at horse farm) but I couldn't care less.  Usually in the parking lot I see a wide array of $70,000+ cars which also thumb their noses at me for driving a "lowly" fiero.  Anyway, I was coming in today and a guy in a Jaguar XKR convertible was coming out when I was going in, so we passed eachother.  Well he stared at me and his jaw seemed to drop.  So I thought to myself that it was pretty cool someone in a $80,000 jaguar was impressed (apparently) with my fiero.  So I pull into a parking space, forgetting which neighborhood I was in I removed my stereo and put all valuables behind my seat (lol), and when I looked up to open my door, the Jaguar guy pulled right next to me.  He gets out and starts talking to me about my fiero.  Come to find out he used to own an '88 GT t-top like mine but he sold it due to a bad back.  He was really impressed!  Needless to say, I was very interested in his jag too.  Man those things are sweet.  But anyway, I love how people still like fiero's, I mean, what other car would make this guy turn around and go back to talk to the owner? He wasn't shocked though when I told him how many clubs there are still around and how many people still love them.  He said if he could find a fountain of youth, the first thing he would buy when he came back would be a fiero!  This is coming from a guy with an XKR!  I asked though he said he would still keep his jag... <P>just thought I would share the experience...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000001||Greg Piet||10-15-2000||10:18 PM||||I get lots of people talking to me about my Fiero, and it is in sorry shape as far as looks go (not nearly as purdy as others I have seen in town)...<P>People see the numbers and the SCCA stickers and  just start chatting away, and I am very nice to them as well...  They like the idea of a Fiero doing the autocrosses and always wish me luck and many tell me to kick some jap ass for them.   <P>Lots of people I think secretly love Fieros!||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||10-15-2000||11:44 PM||||I know how you feel when a Fiero gets attention.  Last week we went out to a fancy restaurant in down town Denver (the Palm for those who are familiar with Denver).  The valet said, “that’s in really good condition.”  When I got my car back a different valet said, “Is that one of those with the V6.  They are really nice cars.”  By the way, it was a company function.   I can’t see paying $50 a plate just to eat.  But it was good.||||reg||1
